Finding 1: OVERALL WINNER
  D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. achieves the lowest average MSE (0.0795) across
  all 64 scenarios in this incidence config.

Finding 2: DOMINANCE
  D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. beats the runner-up (D3: Sat. Quadrants) in 48.4% of scenarios.
  D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. beats the worst performer (D1: Checkerboard) in 98.4% of scenarios.

Finding 3: ROBUSTNESS
  D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. loses rank 1 at Rho = 0.01, 0.2 (rank 2 there).
  D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. loses rank 1 at Gamma = 0.5, 0.7 (rank 2 there).

Finding 4: COVERAGE
  D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. achieves average coverage of 0.942 (nominal = 0.95).
  D1: Checkerboard (worst) achieves coverage of 0.547.

Finding 5: SENSITIVITY
  For D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q., the most influential parameter is Spillover_Type (eta-sq = 0.877),
  followed by Neighbor_Type (eta-sq = 0.043).
  Low-impact parameters (eta-sq < 0.05): Neighbor_Type, Gamma, Rho.

Finding 6: PRACTICAL RECOMMENDATION
  Under Spatial (rho_X = 0.20) incidence, use D8: Inc.-Guided Sat. Q. for treatment assignment.
  It offers the best MSE (9.8x lower than worst performer),
  maintains near-nominal coverage, and is robust across parameter variations.


